.TH WORKSPACE-ZONES 7 "2026-08-20" "waybar-workspace-buttons" "Hyprland"
.SH NAME
workspace-zones \- per-workspace scratch zones for Hyprland
.SH DESCRIPTION
workspace-zones is a Hyprland plugin that gives every numeric workspace its
own scratch zone: workspace
.I N
owns
.IR special:N .
Leaving a workspace closes its zone automatically, no matter how the switch
happened (keybind, bar click,
.BR hyprctl ).
Named specials such as
.I special:magic
are never touched.
.PP
The plugin lives in the waybar-workspace-buttons repository.
On Arch the
.B waybar-workspace-buttons
package installs
.I /usr/lib/hyprland/plugins/libworkspace-zones.so
built against extra/hyprland. hyprland-git and Fedora still need
.BR hyprpm ,
because the plugin is ABI-locked to the running compositor.
The packaged Waybar CFFI module only draws the
has-special dot on workspace buttons; that dot is what these zones were
built for.
.SH INSTALLATION
.nf
# Arch extra/hyprland: already in the package.
# hyprland-git or Fedora:
hyprpm add https://github.com/MasonRhodesDev/waybar-workspace-buttons
hyprpm enable workspace-zones
.fi
.PP
hypr-DE loads a
.I ~/.local/lib/hyprland-plugins/libworkspace-zones.so
override if present, otherwise the packaged path, inside a pcall so a
missing plugin does not abort the rest of the config.
.SH BINDINGS
The plugin requires Hyprland 0.56 or newer with the Lua config
.RI ( hyprland.lua ),
the only supported configuration. Classic
.I zones:*
string dispatchers no longer exist: Hyprland's 0.56 keybinds refactor removed
string dispatchers compositor-wide. The plugin registers first-party
functions under
.BR hl.plugin.zones :
.PP
.nf
hl.bind("SUPER + ALT + S",         function() hl.plugin.zones.toggle() end)
hl.bind("SUPER + ALT + SHIFT + S", function() hl.plugin.zones.move() end)
hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ALT + S",  function() hl.plugin.zones.movesilent() end)
.fi
.PP
hypr-DE ships those Lua binds. Closures resolve at keypress time; if the
plugin is missing, the press logs a Lua error instead of silently doing
nothing.
.TP
.B hl.plugin.zones.toggle()
Show or hide this workspace's zone.
.TP
.B hl.plugin.zones.move()
Send the focused window to the zone and follow it.
.TP
.B hl.plugin.zones.movesilent()
Stash the focused window without following.
.SH NAMED SCRATCHPAD
The global scratchpad
.I special:magic
(hypr-DE:
.B SUPER+S
/
.BR SUPER+0 )
is built-in Hyprland, not this plugin. To dismiss
.I named
specials on workspace switches, set Hyprland's
.B binds:hide_special_on_workspace_change = true
(no plugin needed). That is scoped to the target workspace's monitor: a
special open on another monitor stays.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B plugin:workspace-zones:auto_dismiss
Default 1. Set to 0 to keep zones open across workspace switches.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hypr-de (7),
.BR hypr-de-help (1)
